%%% Sharat's clean references starts here
%% using {{}} in the title preserves casing. i try to use the version that appears in the official pdf of the published paper, unless the title is ALL CAPS. then i use common sense to only capitalize first letter of important words in the title
%% for the venues, i try to find the iteration number, e.g., the 66th Symposium on Foundations of Computer Science
%% conferences should be mentioned as Proceedings of blah
%% journals are just listed by their names
%% since most papers are read digitally these days, it's a good habit to list the doi. this creates a link in the reference. once you click on the link, the url resolves itself based on the doi. 

